# s6_plaintext_free_early_trim: plaintext model released before the parse, pages returned.
#
# basis      s6_plaintext_free_early (17.08., n=3) released 433,255,432 B:
#              conversion hump   s5 2,048,432 / 2,055,244 / 2,061,096
#                                s6 2,054,864 / 2,048,264 / 2,059,988   UNCHANGED
#              inference hump    s5 2,047,080 / 2,072,904 / 2,053,316
#                                s6 2,126,180 / 2,091,784 / 2,105,192   ROSE 2 to 4%
#              published peak    2,061,096 -> 2,105,192                 +2.14%, so it is a REGRESSION
#            LEVER|plaintext_free_early_cpu|released_plaintext_bytes=433255432 fired; pages stayed in the
#            arena (cf. param_stream_cpu: 866 MB for -0.74%, anon:[heap] 383.6 -> 555.3 MB).
# lever      + malloc_trim(0) after the release. A trim after one named release returns that release's
#            pages (as embed_chunk_cpu); global MALLOC_TRIM_THRESHOLD_=0 refused (heap -1,044 MB, anon
#            +788 MB).
# expected   conversion hump -~433 MB (~1.62 GB); peak ~2.05 GB on the inference hump (0 to -1%).
#            Separates "not reducible" from "release did not reach the kernel".
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_early_trim_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16"
